{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Combined multi-queue/request/holder/shared-dependency/staging/GC safety at independent durable-effect boundaries; bounded exploration and arbitrary finite-history induction. Native projection, complete protocol implementation and liveness remain open.",
  "runtime_changes": "None. All production and build inputs match the prior installed journal-append wheel. New proof/model files and one integration regression only. No cumulative zero-overhead or throughput claim.",
  "closed_obligation": "Establish composable model invariants for multiple requests/queues/shared dependencies/repeated recovery, with finite and arbitrary-history results reported separately. This does not close native refinement or the broader distributed-protocol section.",
  "properties": [
    "Every active request has its complete dependency recipe in its queue ownership; all protected objects remain present and outside tombstones.",
    "Durable accepted receipts are immutable, accept counts remain one, ready queues have accurate cached receipts, conflicting retry digests are rejected without requiring retained payloads.",
    "An already consumed handoff is a complete stutter even after a new staging generation.",
    "Receipts require durable deletion; tombstones persist after reclamation.",
    "A concrete proved history contains two queue-scoped equal IDs, lost apply, recovery, restaging, old cleanup replay and retirement of only one queue.",
    "Actual catalog eligibility excludes a live request dependency only under an explicitly caller-established root correspondence."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Complete immutable publication recipes and initially durable names are inputs; actual publication/closure computation is not proved by this model.",
    "Queue namespaces and fencing are explicit obligations; no stale lease/epoch or model-checkpoint/cursor proof is added.",
    "DurableHandoff separately expands uncertain WAL fragments for one handoff; its refinement into this composition and native CommitIo/BatchIo/File/lock mapping are not proved.",
    "TLA finite and Verus unbounded models express related core transitions, not a mechanically verified translation.",
    "No fairness, stabilization or liveness property is claimed.",
    "Retirement is monotone in this composition; rewind/reactivation is not modeled. Initial immutable recipes are supplied, not discovered or published by this model."
  ],
